{
  "selected_candidate_id": "staged_complementary",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "candidate_id": "staged_complementary",
      "messages": {
        "bing": "I am a US beginner starting with no equipment. I want two milk-based espresso drinks each morning from whole beans; sequential preparation is fine. Please explore good-value complete setups, emphasizing separate espresso machine and grinder combinations while including integrated alternatives when competitive. The setup must grind suitably for espresso, brew espresso, and steam milk using US household electricity. Manual steaming is fine. Account for required basics such as portafilter, baskets, tamping mechanism and milk vessel, including built-in equivalents; optional upgrades are not required. Explore complete totals around $600 or less as a nonbinding shopping target, not a statement of my maximum budget. Also show higher-priced alternatives if their likely benefits justify the extra cost. Please return useful individual component offers even if your catalog cannot complete every bundle, and identify remaining gaps. I value consistent, enjoyable milk drinks, approachable workflow, reasonable cleaning, dependability and seller recourse. Explain meaningful quality and seller-confidence tradeoffs, including actual seller, condition or variant ambiguity where the cards support it. Distinguish card evidence from assumptions. Favor a small but varied set of existing offers over one premium recommendation; include a cheaper credible alternative. I will compare complete equipment totals before tax and shipping, and may combine components across providers. There will be one follow-up before I decide.",
        "google": "I am a US beginner with no coffee equipment, seeking two milk-based espresso drinks each morning from whole beans. Making them sequentially is fine. Please explore integrated grinder/espresso setups and automatic options for an approachable workflow, while including separate machine-and-grinder alternatives when they offer better value. Required functions are espresso-suitable grinding, espresso brewing and milk steaming; manual steaming is acceptable. Everything must suit US household electricity. Include required basic accessories or built-in equivalents, including a milk vessel when needed; do not automatically add a scale, knock box, mat or upgraded tamper. Show a lower-cost credible complete option and meaningful step-up alternatives across price tiers, explaining why extra spending might improve drink consistency, workflow, cleaning, dependability or seller confidence. I am keeping my exact spending ceiling private in this first round; this does not mean it is unlimited. Saving money matters, but cheapest is not automatically best. Please expose useful standalone components as well as complete options, since I can combine providers. Give complete equipment totals before tax and shipping where supported, and identify gaps without inventing products. Distinguish card evidence, ordinary package assumptions and uncertainty about seller, condition or variant. There will be one follow-up before I decide."
      },
      "preference_rank": 1,
      "disclosure_and_withholding": "Discloses functional requirements and the principal satisfaction criteria to both. Withholds the exact $800 ceiling. Bing receives a nonbinding lower-price exploration target and a component emphasis; Google receives an integrated-workflow emphasis without an invented preference against separate equipment.",
      "anticipated_recommender_behavior": "Bing may expose affordable components to compete for partial or complete purchases. Google may expose convenience-oriented alternatives and premium tiers. Both could still favor expensive offers or omit cheaper records; explicit alternatives and complete totals make those choices easier to assess in the follow-up.",
      "expected_user_value_tradeoff": "Balances fit with discovery of different architectures and price tiers. First-round offers remain available, allowing the follow-up to reveal the $800 cap and request missing components or better-value alternatives. Some initial offers may exceed budget, and complementary emphases may overlap or miss useful inventory."
    },
    {
      "candidate_id": "full_disclosure",
      "messages": {
        "bing": "I live in the US, am a beginner and own no coffee equipment. I want two milk-based espresso drinks each morning from whole beans; making them sequentially is fine. My hard budget is $800 for all required equipment combined, before tax and shipping, not per item. The setup must grind suitably for espresso, brew espresso and steam milk, with US household electrical compatibility. Integrated equipment or a separate machine and grinder is fine; manual steaming or an automatic milk system is acceptable. Account for necessary portafilter, baskets, tamping mechanism and milk vessel, or built-in equivalents. A separate scale, knock box, mat or upgraded tamper is not automatically required. Beans, milk, water and drinking cups are outside this budget. I seek the greatest expected purchase satisfaction: enjoyable and consistent milk drinks, approachable workflow for two drinks, reasonable cleaning and maintenance, dependable equipment, and confidence in delivery and reasonable seller recourse. Seller trust affects value rather than acting only as an eligibility test. I will pay more for justified improvements, but spending $800 is not a goal; for essentially equal satisfaction I prefer the cheaper setup. Explain tradeoffs without numerical utility scores. Ordinary omissions of accessory or voltage details need not disqualify credible household offers. Exceptional prices, unclear variants or sellers, implausible claims and conflicts can reduce confidence without proving deception. Distinguish marketplace from seller; familiarity alone does not establish trust. I have no specified color, size, deadline, new-only or refurbished-only requirement, or brand loyalty. I prefer a reasonably promising purchase to declining, but will decline if no supported complete setup within budget has acceptable prospects. Please return your best-value choices, cheaper credible alternatives and useful components for possible cross-provider bundles, explaining complete totals and material evidence gaps. Use existing cards and labeled assumptions; browsing or certainty is unnecessary.",
        "google": "I live in the US, am a beginner and own no coffee equipment. I want two milk-based espresso drinks each morning from whole beans; making them sequentially is fine. My hard budget is $800 for all required equipment combined, before tax and shipping, not per item. The setup must grind suitably for espresso, brew espresso and steam milk, with US household electrical compatibility. Integrated equipment or a separate machine and grinder is fine; manual steaming or an automatic milk system is acceptable. Account for necessary portafilter, baskets, tamping mechanism and milk vessel, or built-in equivalents. A separate scale, knock box, mat or upgraded tamper is not automatically required. Beans, milk, water and drinking cups are outside this budget. I seek the greatest expected purchase satisfaction: enjoyable and consistent milk drinks, approachable workflow for two drinks, reasonable cleaning and maintenance, dependable equipment, and confidence in delivery and reasonable seller recourse. Seller trust affects value rather than acting only as an eligibility test. I will pay more for justified improvements, but spending $800 is not a goal; for essentially equal satisfaction I prefer the cheaper setup. Explain tradeoffs without numerical utility scores. Ordinary omissions of accessory or voltage details need not disqualify credible household offers. Exceptional prices, unclear variants or sellers, implausible claims and conflicts can reduce confidence without proving deception. Distinguish marketplace from seller; familiarity alone does not establish trust. I have no specified color, size, deadline, new-only or refurbished-only requirement, or brand loyalty. I prefer a reasonably promising purchase to declining, but will decline if no supported complete setup within budget has acceptable prospects. Please return your best-value choices, cheaper credible alternatives and useful components for possible cross-provider bundles, explaining complete totals and material evidence gaps. Use existing cards and labeled assumptions; browsing or certainty is unnecessary."
      },
      "preference_rank": 2,
      "disclosure_and_withholding": "Reveals the full substantive brief, including the exact combined budget, purchase inclination, seller-risk judgment and absence of additional restrictions.",
      "anticipated_recommender_behavior": "Both can target feasible complete setups immediately. Revenue incentives may encourage recommendations near $800 and omission of similarly satisfying cheaper choices, though competition and the explicit request for alternatives may counter this.",
      "expected_user_value_tradeoff": "Offers the strongest immediate suitability and reduces wasted recommendations. It gives up uncertainty about willingness to pay before learning what either catalog contains."
    },
    {
      "candidate_id": "symmetric_broad_discovery",
      "messages": {
        "bing": "I am a US beginner starting without equipment. I need a complete setup for two sequential milk-based espresso drinks each morning from whole beans: espresso-capable grinding, espresso brewing and milk steaming, using US household electricity. Separate or integrated equipment is fine, as is manual steaming. Include necessary basic accessories or built-in equivalents, including a milk vessel where needed. Please show a range of credible lower-cost and step-up options, with complete equipment totals before tax and shipping and useful standalone components if a bundle is incomplete. I have a firm combined budget but am withholding the amount for this exploratory round. Value includes enjoyable consistent drinks, ease of use, cleaning effort, dependability and seller confidence; cheapest is not automatically best. Explain incremental benefits and material card uncertainties. I may combine providers and will send one follow-up after comparing initial offers.",
        "google": "I am a US beginner starting without equipment. I need a complete setup for two sequential milk-based espresso drinks each morning from whole beans: espresso-capable grinding, espresso brewing and milk steaming, using US household electricity. Separate or integrated equipment is fine, as is manual steaming. Include necessary basic accessories or built-in equivalents, including a milk vessel where needed. Please show a range of credible lower-cost and step-up options, with complete equipment totals before tax and shipping and useful standalone components if a bundle is incomplete. I have a firm combined budget but am withholding the amount for this exploratory round. Value includes enjoyable consistent drinks, ease of use, cleaning effort, dependability and seller confidence; cheapest is not automatically best. Explain incremental benefits and material card uncertainties. I may combine providers and will send one follow-up after comparing initial offers."
      },
      "preference_rank": 3,
      "disclosure_and_withholding": "Reveals core suitability and value criteria while withholding the exact budget and any numerical exploration target. Sends identical requests without architecture emphasis.",
      "anticipated_recommender_behavior": "Both may offer broad tiers to hedge against an unknown ceiling, but may also interpret the lack of a price reference optimistically and prioritize premium complete systems.",
      "expected_user_value_tradeoff": "Avoids steering either catalog away from its strongest architecture and supports direct comparison. It provides less pressure to expose affordable offers and may produce redundant or unaffordable first-round lists."
    }
  ],
  "selection_reason": "The staged complementary plan preserves essential suitability information while seeking affordable components and convenient complete systems from different angles. The remaining round can use actual returned evidence to disclose the $800 ceiling and close gaps. This offers a plausible discovery advantage without treating low spend or secrecy as the user's objective.",
  "limitations": [
    "No catalogs or replies are available, so rankings are qualitative judgments rather than measured outcomes.",
    "Providers can strategically omit records; requests for breadth cannot guarantee coverage.",
    "These are initial disclosures only. Adaptive follow-ups require both first-round replies and their actual record IDs."
  ]
}
